Design a class in Python for a multilingual digital diary entry which supports at least three different languages (English, French, Spanish). Incorporate the functionality to display date and time in different formats (both 12-hour and 24-hour). The class should allow input for title, entry text, mood and weather details. Additionally, design a method that uses a sentiment analysis API to analyze the mood of the diary entry. Include appropriate error handling and data validation for all inputs.

<<Multilingual Digital Diary Manager>>

To satisfy the requirements, the following Python implementation provides a robust structure for managing diary entries.

```python
import datetime

class MultilingualDiaryEntry:
    # Localization dictionary for UI elements
    LABELS = {
        'en': {'date': 'Date', 'mood': 'Mood', 'weather': 'Weather'},
        'fr': {'date': 'Date', 'mood': 'Humeur', 'weather': 'Météo'},
        'es': {'date': 'Fecha', 'mood': 'Estado de ánimo', 'weather': 'Clima'}
    }

    def __init__(self, title, text, mood, weather, lang='en'):
        if not all([title, text, mood, weather]):
            raise ValueError("All diary fields must be provided.")
        if lang not in self.LABELS:
            raise ValueError("Unsupported language.")

        self.title = title
        self.text = text
        self.mood = mood
        self.weather = weather
        self.lang = lang
        self.timestamp = datetime.datetime.now()

    def get_formatted_time(self, use_24h=True):
        """Returns date and time string based on format preference."""
        fmt = "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M" if use_24h else "%Y-%m-%d %I:%M %p"
